issues.body:
`Java_me_magnum_melonds_MelonDSiNand_listTitles` in `app/src/main/cpp/MelonDSNandJNI.cpp` leaves about 5 JNI local references per DSiWare title. `getTitleData` is a plain C++ function, so those refs stay until `listTitles` returns to Java.

for (...) {
    jobject titleData = getTitleData(env, category, titleId);
    env->CallVoidMethod(jniTitleList, listAddMethod, index++, titleData);
}

Each `getTitleData` call creates a `NewByteArray` icon, a `FindClass` for `DSiWareTitle`, two `NewStringUTF` strings, and the `NewObject` result. `ArrayList.add` stores the title and does not free any of those refs. Nothing in the file calls `DeleteLocalRef` or `PopLocalFrame`.

ART's usual local-ref limit is 512. A NAND usually has only a few to a few dozen titles in category `0x00030004`, so this will not overflow. About 100 titles in that category can fill the table.

The returned `ArrayList` must not be deleted. After `add`, delete `titleData`. Inside `getTitleData`, delete the class, both strings, and the icon array only after `NewObject` has stored them.
